{
  "slug": "windows-11-no-sound-after-update",
  "title": "Windows 11 No Sound After Update? 7 Ways to Get It Back",
  "description": "Windows 11 has no sound after an update? Run 7 fixes, from the output device to a driver rollback and a Windows update removal.",
  "category": "PC Troubleshooting",
  "tags": [
    "Windows",
    "PC Maintenance",
    "Troubleshooting",
    "Beginner Guide"
  ],
  "url": "https://www.techtips.fun/blog/windows-11-no-sound-after-update/",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "title": "Windows 11 No Sound After Update? 7 Ways to Get It Back",
      "subtitle": "Windows 11 has no sound after an update? Run 7 fixes, from the output device to a driver…",
      "image": {
        "src": "post-media/windows-11-no-sound-after-update/01-windows-11-no-sound-after-update.webp",
        "width": 1536,
        "height": 1024
      },
      "durationInFrames": 183
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Before You Start",
      "body": "Save your open work. Test your speakers or headphones on another device. If the sound works on the other device, continue with Fix 1.",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 1: Select the Output Device and the Volume",
      "body": "Windows can select the wrong output device after an update. Windows can also set the volume of one app to…",
      "image": {
        "src": "post-media/windows-11-no-sound-after-update/02-windows-11-no-sound-fix1-output-device.webp",
        "width": 1332,
        "height": 756
      },
      "durationInFrames": 366
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 2: Run the Audio Troubleshooter",
      "body": "Windows has a troubleshooter that repairs common sound errors. The Get Help app contains the same…",
      "image": {
        "src": "post-media/windows-11-no-sound-after-update/03-windows-11-no-sound-fix2-troubleshooter.webp",
        "width": 1332,
        "height": 756
      },
      "durationInFrames": 332
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 3: Restart the Audio Services",
      "body": "Every sound on Windows runs through two services: Windows Audio and Windows Audio Endpoint Builder.",
      "image": {
        "src": "post-media/windows-11-no-sound-after-update/04-windows-11-no-sound-fix3-audio-services.webp",
        "width": 1366,
        "height": 765
      },
      "durationInFrames": 320
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 4: Turn Off Audio Enhancements and Spatial Sound",
      "body": "Audio enhancements can stop the sound after a driver update. Spatial sound can also block the output. Open Settings. Select System > Sound.",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 5: Roll Back the Audio Driver",
      "body": "The update can install a faulty driver. Windows stores the earlier driver on the computer.",
      "image": {
        "src": "post-media/windows-11-no-sound-after-update/05-windows-11-no-sound-fix5-device-manager.webp",
        "width": 1366,
        "height": 768
      },
      "durationInFrames": 332
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 6: Reinstall the Audio Driver",
      "body": "Windows installs a new driver after the restart. The driver from the computer manufacturer can work better than the Windows driver.",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
    {
      "type": "outro",
      "heading": "Read the full article",
      "body": "New posts every week on the blog.",
      "url": "techtips.fun",
      "durationInFrames": 165
    }
  ],
